# Allowlist for check-sql-literals.sh.
#
# One line per KNOWN, STILL-OPEN defect that the lint correctly reports.
# Format:  <path-relative-to-src>|<KIND>|<detail>  # why it is here
# The key deliberately has no line number, so it survives edits elsewhere
# in the file.
#
# Adding a line needs the same justification as raising a ratchet
# baseline: it makes a real defect invisible to CI. Every entry is
# reprinted loudly on every run, and an entry that stops matching is
# reported as stale so it gets deleted when the bug is fixed.
#
# Get the key for a finding with:
#   sh scripts/check-sql-literals.sh --keys
# Verify the true state of the tree, ignoring this file, with:
#   sh scripts/check-sql-literals.sh --strict
#
# CURRENTLY EMPTY. It was created 2026-08-10 with one entry —
# MonsterKillQuest::save()'s `executeQuery("-_-")`, which is how this gate
# proved itself on a live defect — and that entry was deleted the same day
# because the defect was fixed. Zero entries is the state to keep it in.
